# Overview 
the sorter discord bot should include all functionality of sorter web for use in a discord context. It should be able to be added to any arbitrary discord server. It will allow users in a server to, from within any text channel, use the /tag command to create & link that channel with a sorter tag. After this is done, users within the channel can use a specific (sorter emoji) Reaction on any message to add it as an item within the already created tag. (also with a /item command, but the reaction is the main way). Once an item is added, it can be voted on, and its ranking is shown (approximately) to all users (not sure yet how this will be implemented--more reactions of custom emojis that show podium ranking (ie medals) then numbers for rank position, or something else.)
to vote within a channel/tag, user uses /vote, which begins the voting. then need a way to display the two messages (ideally side by side, but that will by pretty irritating, so if we can't do that its ok) and get from user a vote with a MAGNITUDE -- ie on a scale of -100, 100 on item1, item2, vote could be 32 meaning item2 by that much. 

Users can OPTIONALLY link their sorter account to their discord account via oauth using /link in discord. This will use `http{s}://{hostname based on .env variable 'HOSTNAME'}/api/auth/discord` endpoint from our api. 
If a user has NOT linked their discord account, they can still interact fully, and their actions will be recorded under a temporary user based on their discord username / identifier. This should be added to the database in the standard users table with the username being '@discord_{their username}'. Optionally later this user can choose to create a linked sorter account, also using /link. the "pseudo-user" created from their discord identifier that already exists for them should be updated to be their new user, but the user's account creation flow should be the same otherwise, and should occur on the sorter website. 

We should use discord embeds deeply, as well as custom buttons & views where they can be appropriately leveraged. Same with emoji reactions. Additionally we need to support sharding well. 

We will be TypeScript, discord.js, and 'Discord Bot TypeScript Template', which may optionally have its structure included. Follow the structure and setup that it uses whenever possible, as well as best practices that discord recommends themselves for developers. 

